#align(center)[#text(size: 17pt, weight: "bold")[NARRATOR NOTES - DO NOT RECORD]]
#v(0.9em)

Record the chapter numbers and chapter titles. Do not record this notes page. The manuscript contains no retailer-specific review request or promotional back matter.

#v(0.7em)

#block(width: 100%, stroke: 0.9pt + luma(100), inset: (x: 12pt, y: 10pt), radius: 3pt)[
  #text(size: 12pt, weight: "bold")[OCTOBER 2026 REVISION - READ FIRST]

  Four small continuity fixes were made after the July copy. In this PDF the changed paragraphs are highlighted in yellow. Re-record the highlighted passages in the order they appear here; every other word is identical to the July copy. (The two moved Chapter Two paragraphs beginning "On the word threads" and "His notes, though" may be spliced from your existing takes if you prefer - their words did not change, only their position.)

  + *Chapter Two* - paragraph beginning "The shop opened at ten": the long drive home is now the long walk home. Callie walks to the auction in Chapter One and owns no car in this book.
  + *Chapter Two* - paragraph beginning "She sold almost nothing": was "She sold nothing," which clashed with the birthday gift she wraps in the same paragraph.
  + *Chapter Two* - the exchange beginning "No." Mae smiled: restructured so Mae's hands go still on the word "threads" instead of two paragraphs later. Three highlighted paragraphs are read in the new order shown.
  + *Chapter Seven ("The Reckoning")* - paragraph beginning "Not the bell. The knock": Callie now puts on her coat before answering the door, so her taking it off later in the scene tracks.
]

